{"name":"Clinker","hex":"#463623","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Clinker","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Clinker"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cement clinker","blocks":[{"text":"Cement clinker is a solid material produced as an intermediary product in Portland cement manufacturing. Clinker occurs as lumps or nodules, usually 3 millimetres (0.12 in) to 25 millimetres (0.98 in) in diameter. It is produced by sintering limestone and aluminosilicate materials such as clay during the cement kiln stage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/LDClinkerScaled.jpg/330px-LDClinkerScaled.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cement_clinker"},{"title":"Clinker (boat building)","blocks":[{"text":"Clinker-built, also known as lapstrake-built, is a method of boat building in which the edges of longitudinal (lengthwise-running) hull planks overlap each other."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Clinker-carvel.svg/330px-Clinker-carvel.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clinker_(boat_building)"},{"title":"Clinker (waste)","blocks":[{"text":"Clinker is a generic name given to waste from industrial processes, particularly those that involve smelting metals, welding, burning fossil fuels and use of a blacksmith's forge, which commonly causes a large buildup of clinker around the tuyere. Clinker often forms a loose, dark deposit consisting of waste materials such as coke, coal, slag, charcoal, and grit. Clinker often has a glassy look to it, usually because of the formation of molten silica compounds during processing. Clinker generally is much denser than coke, and, unlike coke, generally contains too little carbon to be of any value as fuel. It is also applied to the byproduct of combustion and heating by those who use anthracite or lignite coal-fired boilers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/%DA%A9%D9%84%DB%8C%D9%86%DA%A9%D8%B1_%D8%B3%DB%8C%D9%85%D8%A7%D9%86.JPG/330px-%DA%A9%D9%84%DB%8C%D9%86%DA%A9%D8%B1_%D8%B3%DB%8C%D9%85%D8%A7%D9%86.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clinker_(waste)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Hot_Clinker_2.jpg/500px-Hot_Clinker_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Hot_Clinker_2.jpg/500px-Hot_Clinker_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hot clinker","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHot_Clinker_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Clinker_built_dinghy_awaiting_restoration.jpg/500px-Clinker_built_dinghy_awaiting_restoration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Clinker_built_dinghy_awaiting_restoration.jpg/1280px-Clinker_built_dinghy_awaiting_restoration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Clinker_built_dinghy_awaiting_restoration.jpg/500px-Clinker_built_dinghy_awaiting_restoration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clinker built dinghy showing some of the basic structural details. The single rowing thwart supports the after end of the centre-board case. The pairs of knees at each end of the thwart can be seen; also the longitudinal stringer (rising) on which the thwart rests.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClinker_built_dinghy_awaiting_restoration.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Nydam-Boot.JPG/500px-Nydam-Boot.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Nydam-Boot.JPG/1280px-Nydam-Boot.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Nydam-Boot.JPG/500px-Nydam-Boot.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Nydam boat, an early example of clinker construction.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANydam-Boot.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Gokstadskipet1.jpg/500px-Gokstadskipet1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Gokstadskipet1.jpg/1280px-Gokstadskipet1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Gokstadskipet1.jpg/500px-Gokstadskipet1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Gokstad Ship, a Viking longship, displaying the overlapping planks that characterize clinker construction.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGokstadskipet1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Sailors_of_HMS_King_Edward_VII%E2%80%A6.jpg/500px-Sailors_of_HMS_King_Edward_VII%E2%80%A6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Sailors_of_HMS_King_Edward_VII%E2%80%A6.jpg/1280px-Sailors_of_HMS_King_Edward_VII%E2%80%A6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Sailors_of_HMS_King_Edward_VII%E2%80%A6.jpg/500px-Sailors_of_HMS_King_Edward_VII%E2%80%A6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm